The powerset-of-four-tokens neighbourhood system (nonempty subsets).

<!-- formalization -->
**Definition (`Token`).** The token set is a four-element type, standing for $\Delta=\{0,1,2,3\}$.

**Definition (`P4Mem`).** A subset belongs to the family precisely when it is nonempty.

**Theorem (`P4_inter_mem`).** If $Z$ is nonempty and $Z\subseteq X\cap Y$, then $X\cap Y$ is nonempty.

*Proof.* Nonemptiness passes along the inclusion. ∎

**Definition (`master`).** The master set is the full set of tokens.

**Theorem (`P4_master_mem`), (`P4_master_nonempty`).** The master is nonempty (hence a neighbourhood).

*Proof.* The full token set is nonempty. ∎

**Theorem (`P4_sub_master`).** Every neighbourhood is contained in the master.

*Proof.* Every set of tokens lies in the full token set. ∎

**Definition (`neighborhoodSystem`).** The neighbourhood system on the four-token carrier whose members are exactly the nonempty subsets, with this master set.

*Proof.* The master is nonempty and a neighbourhood; every neighbourhood lies in the master; if two neighbourhoods meet in a set containing a third neighbourhood, their intersection is nonempty by the preceding theorem, hence again a neighbourhood. ∎

